# guanhe-mcp v0.5.0

Model Context Protocol (stdio) server that wraps the GuanHe **readonly** Agent HTTP API — `/api/v1/agent` (feed, search, reports) and `/api/v2/agent` (semantic / vector RAG).

## What it gives you

Three families of read-only tools over your GuanHe data:

1. **Feed & search** — time-ordered Twitter / YouTube / news items with keyword, ticker, tag, people, and country filters.
2. **Reports** — daily / weekly digests and market / theme reports, delivered as a public `share_url`.
3. **Semantic RAG** — concept-level vector search over uploaded documents and long-form content.

## Reports

The three report tools (`report_latest`, `report_by_date`, `report_list`) share a `kind` parameter. v0.5.0 supports five canonical kinds:

| `kind` | Report | `report_by_date` key |
|---|---|---|
| `twitter_daily` | Twitter feed daily digest | report_date |
| `youtube_daily` | YouTube feed daily digest | report_date |
| `market_daily` | Daily market report (index performers, ETF performance) | report_date |
| `market_weekly` | Weekly market report (stored on OSS) | **week_end** (Friday) |
| `theme` | Theme performance report (constituent returns per investment theme) | report_date |

> **All reports return only a `share_url`** — a public, no-auth URL that opens the fully rendered report in a browser. No report inlines its body (`content_markdown` is always null); hand the `share_url` to the user rather than trying to summarize raw HTML.
>
> Legacy short names `twitter` / `youtube` / `market` are still accepted as aliases and normalize to the canonical form (`twitter_daily` / `youtube_daily` / `market_daily`).

## Requirements

- Python **>= 3.10**
- `httpx` (installed automatically)
- A **Personal Access Token** (`ght_...`) from the web app: **User menu → API Keys**

## Install

```bash
# From the published wheel (recommended for end users):
pip install "https://guanhecapital.hk/downloads/guanhe_mcp-0.5.0-py3-none-any.whl"

# From local source (dev):
cd tools/guanhe-mcp
pip install -e .
```

## Environment variables

| Variable | Required | Description |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| `GUANHE_TOKEN` | Yes | PAT starting with `ght_` |
| `GUANHE_BASE_URL` | Yes | API origin, e.g. `https://your-host` (no trailing slash) |

## Cursor (`~/.cursor/mcp.json`)

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "guanhe": {
      "command": "/path/to/your/python",
      "args": ["-m", "guanhe_mcp.server"],
      "env": {
        "GUANHE_TOKEN": "ght_xxxxxxxx",
        "GUANHE_BASE_URL": "https://www.guanhecapital.hk",
        "PYTHONUNBUFFERED": "1"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Replace `/path/to/your/python` with the output of `which python` (or `where python` on Windows) after activating your target virtual environment.

## Claude Desktop (`claude_desktop_config.json`)

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "guanhe": {
      "command": "/usr/bin/env",
      "args": ["guanhe-mcp"],
      "env": {
        "GUANHE_TOKEN": "ght_xxxxxxxx",
        "GUANHE_BASE_URL": "https://www.guanhecapital.hk"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Tools (12)

### Feed & search (6)

| Tool | Description | Maps to |
|------|-------------|---------|
| `daily_feed` | Time-ordered feed + optional keyword search | `GET /api/v1/agent/daily` |
| `daily_item` | Full content + transcript for one item | `GET /api/v1/agent/daily/{id}` |
| `daily_items_batch` | Full detail for up to 10 items at once | `POST /api/v1/agent/daily/batch` |
| `daily_multi_search` | 1–5 parallel search groups, server-side dedup | `POST /api/v1/agent/daily/multi` |
| `list_subscriptions` | Enabled feed channels with 30-day counts | `GET /api/v1/agent/subscriptions` |
| `list_sources` | Source types, preset membership, 30-day counts | `GET /api/v1/agent/sources` |

### Reports (3)

| Tool | Description | Maps to |
|------|-------------|---------|
| `report_latest` | Latest completed report for a given `kind` | `GET /api/v1/agent/reports/latest?kind=` |
| `report_by_date` | Report for a specific date (`market_weekly` uses week_end Friday) | `GET /api/v1/agent/reports/{date}?kind=` |
| `report_list` | Paginated list of available reports | `GET /api/v1/agent/reports?kind=` |

### Semantic / Vector RAG (3, since v0.3.0)

| Tool | Description | Maps to |
|------|-------------|---------|
| `semantic_search` | Concept-level vector search over uploaded docs & long feeds | `POST /api/v2/agent/semantic-search` |
| `hybrid_search` | RRF-fused keyword + semantic search | `POST /api/v2/agent/hybrid-search` |
| `chunks_by_locator` | Fetch contiguous chunks by chapter / page / chunk index | `POST /api/v2/agent/chunks-by-locator` |

## Which tool should I use?

| You want | Use |
|---|---|
| Recent items on a topic / ticker / person | `daily_feed` |
| Several topic angles in one call (deduped) | `daily_multi_search` |
| Full text of one or a few items | `daily_item` / `daily_items_batch` |
| Today's Twitter / YouTube digest | `report_latest` kind=`twitter_daily` / `youtube_daily` |
| Today's market report | `report_latest` kind=`market_daily` |
| This week's market report | `report_latest` kind=`market_weekly` |
| Theme performance report | `report_latest` kind=`theme` |
| Browse report history | `report_list` |
| Concept keywords can't capture ("value investing methodology") | `semantic_search` |
| Proper noun + concept ("1X Technologies funding strategy") | `hybrid_search` |
| A specific doc section (chapter / page) | `chunks_by_locator` |
| Which channels are subscribed / active | `list_subscriptions` / `list_sources` |

> **Citation rule:** v2 results are chunk-level snippets. Always cite the returned `content_id` so the user can verify in the GuanHe UI.

## Quick usage examples

```bash
# Set env
export GUANHE_TOKEN="ght_..."
export GUANHE_BASE_URL="https://www.guanhecapital.hk"

# Run the server (it reads JSON-RPC from stdin)
python -m guanhe_mcp.server
```

Smoke testing via the fallback script:

```bash
# Feed & search
python scripts/call_guanhe_mcp.py daily_feed '{"since": "24h", "limit": 5}'
python scripts/call_guanhe_mcp.py daily_multi_search '{"groups": [{"q": "NVDA OR 英伟达", "since": "7d"}, {"q": "Greer OR USTR OR 贸易代表", "since": "7d"}]}'

# Reports (kind = canonical)
python scripts/call_guanhe_mcp.py report_latest '{"kind": "market_daily"}'
python scripts/call_guanhe_mcp.py report_latest '{"kind": "market_weekly"}'
python scripts/call_guanhe_mcp.py report_latest '{"kind": "theme"}'
python scripts/call_guanhe_mcp.py report_list '{"kind": "twitter_daily", "limit": 5}'
python scripts/call_guanhe_mcp.py report_by_date '{"kind": "market_weekly", "date": "2026-06-13"}'

# Semantic RAG (v0.3)
python scripts/call_guanhe_mcp.py semantic_search '{"query": "humanoid robot home deployment", "top_k": 5}'
python scripts/call_guanhe_mcp.py hybrid_search '{"query": "1X Technologies NEO funding", "top_k": 5}'
python scripts/call_guanhe_mcp.py chunks_by_locator '{"file_id": 1439, "chapter": "**Timeline of Major Developments:**"}'
```

## Key parameter notes

**`kind`** — report type. Canonical: `twitter_daily`, `youtube_daily`, `market_daily`, `market_weekly`, `theme` (legacy `twitter`/`youtube`/`market` accepted as aliases). See [Reports](#reports).

**`q` syntax** — space = AND (all terms must match), `OR` (uppercase) = any match, `"phrase"` = exact substring.
- Good: `q=NVDA OR 英伟达`
- Bad: `q=帮我找近期美国访华的重要消息` (treated as a literal string, will return 0 results)

**`tickers`** — must include exchange suffix: `NVDA.US`, `9988.HK`, `600519.SS`, `0700.HK`.
If unsure of the suffix, use `q=NVDA` first and read the `tickers` field in the response.

**`people`** — comma-separated person names (OR logic). Use original-form names from content:
`people=Trump,Musk` (not `特朗普`). More precise than `q=Trump` full-text search.
Read the `people` field in list responses to discover valid names.

**`countries`** — comma-separated country **full English names** (OR logic):
`countries=United States,China`. NOT ISO codes (`US` will not match).

**`since`** — `24h`, `48h`, `7d`, `14d`, `30d`, `2w`, or ISO 8601. Invalid values return 400.

**`sources`** — comma-separated: `twitter`, `youtube`, `youtube_feed`, `news`, `pdf`, `image`, `audio`, `text`, `podcast`.
Omit to use your web-app Daily preset.

